"Everything VISIBLE in a menu is modifiable in that menu, intuitively, and menus are consistent with one another: the same kind of thing renders and toggles the same way everywhere. A control that exists but cannot currently be used renders VISIBLY DISABLED (never hidden, never silently inert), and its disablement re-evaluates live -- removing an item can re-enable other items' buttons. Menus only propose: a toggle that has an in-fiction cost queues the corresponding action rather than bypassing it."